WEBVTT

00:01.770 --> 00:05.570
<i>Just what did I get dragged into?</i>

00:06.760 --> 00:10.850
<i>My father grew up as the 
eldest son in a major company,</i>

00:10.850 --> 00:13.000
<i>but he threw away his status 
and went out on his own,</i>

00:13.000 --> 00:15.480
<i>and now runs a traditional 
Japanese restaurant.</i>

00:15.480 --> 00:16.870
<i>Then, one day...</i>

00:16.870 --> 00:19.620
Dad brought up something really weird.

00:17.370 --> 00:19.620
<b>Otonashi Family Inheritance 
Assignment Documents</b>

00:19.910 --> 00:22.750
Rion, I'd like you to do this in my place.

00:23.090 --> 00:27.080
Dad said something about wanting to show 
that he feels remorse for his crime.

00:27.360 --> 00:32.260
He must know something 
specific about Mom's incident.

00:30.980 --> 00:33.130
<b>Otonashi Family Inheritance 
Assignment Documents</b>

00:33.130 --> 00:35.510
If you're able to get 
priority on the inheritance,

00:35.510 --> 00:37.960
you can spend it however you'd like.

01:45.710 --> 01:49.520
<i>The fact that I have someone in my 
family who was a victim in a murder,</i>

01:49.520 --> 01:53.660
<i>the fact that I have to somehow explain 
how my grandfather was behind it,</i>

01:53.660 --> 01:56.700
<i>and the ungodly amount of inheritance... 
None of this makes sense.</i>

01:57.370 --> 02:00.070
<i>Also, I definitely came underdressed...</i>

02:00.070 --> 02:01.430
Well, everyone...

02:01.430 --> 02:02.970
Thanks for gathering here today.

02:02.970 --> 02:04.490
I'm sure you're all

02:04.490 --> 02:09.440
quite wary of me, and you may be 
wondering, "Who the hell are you?"

02:09.680 --> 02:11.780
But please, just think about this.

02:11.780 --> 02:14.070
<i>I'm</i> the one who's the most 
inconvenienced by this.

02:14.070 --> 02:16.700
I'm a complete outsider here,

02:16.700 --> 02:18.700
yet I've been asked to 
take on this bizarre role,

02:18.940 --> 02:21.820
and I've taken time out of 
my day to come all this way.

02:22.110 --> 02:25.030
You might say that I could've just said no,

02:25.030 --> 02:27.830
but could I really say no to 
President Otonashi's request?

02:27.830 --> 02:31.000
He really wants me to rank all of you...

02:31.000 --> 02:34.460
Of course, the one I rank 
the lowest will resent me.

02:34.460 --> 02:38.260
Who knows what they might do in retaliation?

02:38.260 --> 02:41.510
Come, now. None of us would do anything rash.

02:41.510 --> 02:43.380
Our father wouldn't let 
us get away with that.

02:43.380 --> 02:46.970
But I'd rather you not come for 
me after he passes, either.

02:47.210 --> 02:49.770
Right now, the president is quite well,

02:49.770 --> 02:52.520
so it'd be unfavorable if 
I didn't do what I asked.

02:52.520 --> 02:56.750
No matter how this goes, 
it's a lose-lose situation for me.

02:56.750 --> 03:00.680
So why did my grandfather 
choose you, Iwanaga-san?

03:02.300 --> 03:05.580
Did you two not do a background check on me?

03:05.800 --> 03:07.590
I attempted to,

03:07.590 --> 03:11.040
but all the trusted investigation 
companies declined.

03:11.040 --> 03:14.750
Based on that, it's very 
obvious that you're special.

03:14.980 --> 03:19.380
In my case, my nephew was coincidentally 
in the same club as you in high school.

03:19.380 --> 03:22.500
His name is Amachi Manabu. 
Does that ring a bell?

03:22.500 --> 03:25.180
Oh? He was related to the president?

03:25.180 --> 03:28.850
He told me to avoid making 
an enemy of you at all costs.

03:31.910 --> 03:36.380
Anyway, rumors had apparently spread 
about me without my knowledge,

03:36.380 --> 03:39.110
and President Otonashi took a liking to me.

03:39.560 --> 03:43.950
That aside, I don't want any resentment 
from anyone for fulfilling this role.

03:43.950 --> 03:47.510
Kuro-senpai here is not my assistant.

03:47.510 --> 03:50.200
He has been my boyfriend 
ever since high school.

03:50.200 --> 03:51.540
Boyfriend?

03:51.540 --> 03:55.040
My boyfriend and I are staying 
at this lovely hotel.

03:55.040 --> 03:58.050
Naturally, we'd like to enjoy our time here.

03:58.050 --> 04:01.670
The bath in the room we're staying in is huge,

04:01.670 --> 04:03.920
so we can get in together, 
he can "wash his fingers" in my vagina,

04:03.920 --> 04:06.140
and who knows where that might lead—

04:08.090 --> 04:11.280
I do beg your pardon. 
I've made my desires a bit too public.

04:11.280 --> 04:12.600
But I'm sure none of you

04:12.600 --> 04:16.610
want to be constantly jumping at 
shadows until tomorrow, correct?

04:16.610 --> 04:21.190
Yes. And I'd rather not have 
our relationships turn sour.

04:21.530 --> 04:23.780
In that case, I propose an alliance.

04:23.780 --> 04:24.990
An alliance?

04:25.830 --> 04:27.240
What's being requested of you

04:27.520 --> 04:28.920
is that you explain how

04:28.920 --> 04:32.510
President Otonashi killed Otonashi 
Sumi-san twenty-three years ago.

04:32.510 --> 04:34.230
So let's work together to come up with

04:34.230 --> 04:36.830
an answer that the president 
will be satisfied with.

04:36.830 --> 04:41.100
All of you can discuss how you 
want to split up the inheritance,

04:41.100 --> 04:43.340
you'll decide the order that 
best meets your desires,

04:43.340 --> 04:45.800
and we'll report a ranking to the president.

04:45.800 --> 04:50.220
We'll decide the ranking depending on 
how much you've all contributed...

04:50.740 --> 04:55.440
Actually, it'd be a hassle to have to hear 
three separate answers from each of you.

04:55.440 --> 04:57.800
I shall take my leave for about an hour.

04:57.800 --> 05:01.570
Until then, please discuss my proposal.

05:07.490 --> 05:12.410
Is this proposal something Dad came up 
with, or was it Miss Iwanaga herself?

05:12.410 --> 05:16.080
I doubt she'd do something 
the president didn't wish for.

05:16.080 --> 05:19.480
But she honestly seems like she 
wouldn't have a problem doing that.

05:19.480 --> 05:22.420
At the same time, 
her proposal isn't a bad idea.

05:22.420 --> 05:24.130
It makes sense.

05:24.810 --> 05:27.090
And how do you feel about the inheritance?

05:27.090 --> 05:29.640
There are parts of his assets,
as well as rights,

05:29.640 --> 05:31.260
that I'd personally like to have.

05:31.260 --> 05:32.930
If I'm guaranteed those,

05:33.150 --> 05:35.510
I don't care where I rank in this assignment.

05:35.510 --> 05:37.350
What about Kaoruko-neesan?

05:37.350 --> 05:41.140
Kaoruko didn't seem very fond 
of the idea of only you and

05:41.140 --> 05:42.780
Ryoma-san benefiting from this.

05:42.780 --> 05:46.650
Since you've taken over the group, 
the president is very fond of you.

05:46.650 --> 05:48.370
He's also very fond of Ryoma-san,

05:48.370 --> 05:51.910
who decided to have the courage 
to go the exact opposite route.

05:51.910 --> 05:57.210
On the other hand, Kaoruko seems to feel 
that her father doesn't love her very much.

05:57.210 --> 06:00.710
She seems unable to stand the 
fact that this might give you two

06:00.710 --> 06:02.840
an upper hand in the inheritance.

06:03.070 --> 06:07.420
Nee-san just wants the satisfaction 
of winning against my brother and me.

06:07.420 --> 06:10.010
What does Ryoma-san think 
about the inheritance?

06:10.010 --> 06:12.140
There's no point in asking 
my brother about that.

06:12.430 --> 06:14.520
He'd say a huge inheritance 
will just lead to trouble,

06:14.520 --> 06:18.640
so if Rion has anything she wants, 
she should just get as much as she'd like.

06:18.640 --> 06:23.970
Uncle, if you understand my father that 
well, why do you two still not get along?

06:23.970 --> 06:25.610
It's <i>because</i> I understand him.

06:25.910 --> 06:28.860
Nii-san always does things I don't like.

06:28.860 --> 06:31.370
If the eldest brother 
gives up his inheritance,

06:31.370 --> 06:33.390
or if any of us get a 
disproportionate share,

06:33.390 --> 06:35.020
everyone would be suspicious.

06:35.020 --> 06:38.250
There will even be those who 
think this was all my doing.

06:38.250 --> 06:42.450
The amount of trouble I'll have 
to go through to avoid that...

06:42.450 --> 06:45.340
I'm sure Nii-san is quite pleased that 
he gets to stay true to himself.

06:45.660 --> 06:47.210
Er, sorry about this...

06:47.210 --> 06:49.540
Oh, this isn't your fault, Rion.

06:49.540 --> 06:51.180
It's just your father.

06:51.180 --> 06:56.780
Then why don't we rank Uncle Koya first 
so Aunt Kaoruko can regain her dignity,

06:56.780 --> 07:02.690
and the two of you can decide how to split 
the inheritance? Would that be best?

07:02.920 --> 07:04.980
I honestly don't care where I rank.

07:04.980 --> 07:09.180
That's fine with me, since 
it'll probably satisfy Kaoruko.

07:09.180 --> 07:10.070
And you, Susumu-san?

07:10.070 --> 07:15.630
It's much easier than arguing 
over whose answer is the best.

07:15.630 --> 07:18.370
It's not like I want to fight over 
this inheritance to begin with.

07:18.370 --> 07:20.460
Then I guess we've decided.

07:20.460 --> 07:21.140
Yes.

07:21.140 --> 07:21.750
Right.

07:21.750 --> 07:23.990
What a peculiar predicament.

07:23.990 --> 07:27.900
Such a large sum of money is at stake, 
yet everything was decided so peacefully.

07:28.710 --> 07:29.970
I mean...

07:30.200 --> 07:32.430
Did this assignment have 
an answer to begin with?

07:33.330 --> 07:38.360
If Grandfather is the culprit and wants 
to repent by bringing his crime to light,

07:38.360 --> 07:41.440
then it'd be quickest if he 
just told us how he killed her.

07:41.440 --> 07:44.440
So why in the world would 
he make us think about it?

07:44.920 --> 07:47.770
Do you think this assignment 
has another purpose?

07:48.000 --> 07:52.690
Grandfather knows something very special 
and can bring it all to light right now.

07:52.690 --> 07:54.890
Perhaps he's trying to make us realize that.

07:54.890 --> 07:56.990
That's what my father suggested.

07:56.990 --> 07:59.700
Even if we go along with 
Miss Iwanaga's proposal,

07:59.700 --> 08:01.870
there are still a number of questions.

08:01.870 --> 08:04.120
Nah, you're overthinking this.

08:04.120 --> 08:07.260
President Otonashi is indeed 
involved with Sumi-san's death.

08:07.260 --> 08:11.940
But he doesn't think you'd believe him 
if he told you how he killed her...

08:12.610 --> 08:16.090
So he just wanted his children 
to figure out how he did it.

08:16.090 --> 08:18.350
Can we really believe that, thought?

08:18.350 --> 08:19.850
There is an answer.

08:19.850 --> 08:24.010
If you all seek out the truth, 
you'll eventually reach it.

08:24.010 --> 08:27.110
But there's nothing 
suspicious about my father.

08:27.110 --> 08:28.480
Is that so?

08:28.730 --> 08:30.340
For example, when the incident occurred,

08:30.340 --> 08:33.610
there was President Otonashi and those 
he didn't want any suspicion to fall upon.

08:33.610 --> 08:37.410
Isn't it suspicious that Ryoma-san, 
Kaoruko-san, Susumu-san,

08:37.410 --> 08:40.590
and Koya-san all had alibis at the time?

08:40.590 --> 08:43.330
It's as though they're all being protected.

08:43.330 --> 08:48.090
Don't you think the only one capable of 
that at the time was President Otonashi?

08:49.090 --> 08:54.190
The incident happened twenty-three years 
ago, on February 18th at around 7 PM.

08:54.190 --> 08:56.090
Sumi-san was 58 at the time.

08:56.090 --> 08:59.600
<b>Okamoto
Osteopathic Clinic</b>

08:56.420 --> 08:59.600
She had gone to an 
independently-run massage clinic.

08:59.600 --> 09:03.600
It was a fully private service she 
received once a month to relax.

09:03.960 --> 09:07.010
She didn't even have a 
car take her to and from.

09:07.010 --> 09:10.350
And on her way back, 
she was attacked by someone.

09:10.350 --> 09:11.580
Thief!

09:11.580 --> 09:13.450
Someone! That man—

09:14.130 --> 09:18.620
Someone catch that man wearing black! 
He went toward the station!

09:18.620 --> 09:21.620
When the residents went down to 
check after hearing her scream,

09:21.620 --> 09:23.900
Sumi-san was already dead.

09:24.230 --> 09:27.540
Her body was still warm, so it was determined 
that the incident had just occurred.

09:27.780 --> 09:31.080
The cause of death was 
hemorrhagic shock caused by

09:31.080 --> 09:32.850
two stab wounds near her heart.

09:32.850 --> 09:34.680
They don't know who the knife belonged to,

09:34.680 --> 09:36.950
and they weren't able to 
detect any fingerprints.

09:36.950 --> 09:40.100
Sumi-san had a habit of walking 
around with quite a bit of cash.

09:40.330 --> 09:43.210
She always had over a 
million yen in her wallet,

09:43.210 --> 09:46.230
and all of her bills had 
been taken from that wallet.

09:46.230 --> 09:47.940
Burglary and murder.

09:47.940 --> 09:50.290
At first glance, it seems 
to be a simple crime.

09:50.290 --> 09:55.110
The suspect tried to take her 
money and was met with resistance,

09:55.480 --> 09:57.220
so he ended up stabbing her to death.

09:57.220 --> 09:59.990
But the investigation came 
to an immediate standstill

09:59.990 --> 10:01.990
because there was no further evidence.

10:02.240 --> 10:05.460
The police figured it was very 
likely a burglary and murder,

10:05.460 --> 10:08.580
but considered the possibility 
that it was actually a murder

10:08.810 --> 10:11.240
made to <i>look</i> like a burglary and murder,

10:11.240 --> 10:15.210
since Sumi-san had many people who
resented her for her work, as well.

10:15.210 --> 10:18.720
Her family and Koya-san 
also had possible motives.

10:18.720 --> 10:24.110
All of you knew that Sumi-san went 
to the massage clinic once a month,

10:24.110 --> 10:27.600
so it would've been possible that you 
planned to ambush her on her way home.

10:27.990 --> 10:31.160
She was against Kaoruko-san's 
marriage to Koya-san,

10:31.160 --> 10:33.970
and she was against Ryoma-san and 
Susumu-san's desired careers.

10:33.970 --> 10:36.490
President Otonashi felt 
distress from his children

10:36.490 --> 10:38.400
and thought the group was in danger.

10:38.680 --> 10:41.660
There was a reason for all of you to 
think that Sumi-san was in the way.

10:41.660 --> 10:43.900
At the time, my brother and 
I thought it'd be better

10:43.900 --> 10:46.660
if our mother was gone countless times.

10:46.920 --> 10:50.170
I could never get into her good graces.

10:50.170 --> 10:53.890
She even threatened me saying 
that she'd crush the company

10:53.890 --> 10:56.130
I'd started if I didn't 
break up with Kaoruko.

10:56.130 --> 10:58.700
Of course one might consider murdering her.

10:58.700 --> 11:01.170
But because all of you had alibis,

11:01.170 --> 11:03.220
you were immediately cleared of suspicion.

11:03.220 --> 11:05.560
President Otonashi was in another prefecture,

11:05.560 --> 11:09.310
and around 7 PM, he was in a 
meeting with over ten people.

11:09.530 --> 11:11.880
Ryoma-san and Susumu-san 
were at the group HQ,

11:11.880 --> 11:14.760
which was an hour's drive from 
the scene of the incident,

11:14.760 --> 11:19.280
and were spotted arguing there 
around the time of the incident.

11:19.280 --> 11:21.450
We were both young back then.

11:21.770 --> 11:24.780
I was in my twenties, and Nii-san 
had just entered his thirties.

11:24.780 --> 11:29.450
Nii-san had been training as a cook at a 
famous restaurant in secret to our mother,

11:29.450 --> 11:32.290
but that was exposed, and he 
was made to come to the office,

11:32.290 --> 11:34.280
making him overly stressed.

11:34.710 --> 11:38.880
I was only given work as my brother's 
assistant, and it made me annoyed.

11:39.120 --> 11:44.350
My brother was forced to do this 
work, while I wanted to do this work.

11:44.350 --> 11:46.600
Of course we fought over trivial things.

11:46.600 --> 11:51.480
Yes. It seems as though many around you 
knew that you two didn't get along,

11:51.480 --> 11:54.990
but you two hadn't really 
fought at the office prior,

11:54.990 --> 11:57.480
so you ended up with a clear alibi.

11:57.780 --> 12:00.240
It may be coincidental, but quite well done.

12:08.300 --> 12:13.000
<b>The Silenced Children</b>

12:13.430 --> 12:17.210
During the incident, Koya-san was 
also out visiting business partners,

12:17.210 --> 12:21.230
and was in the middle of negotiations, 
so he couldn't leave.

12:21.230 --> 12:23.590
I was 33 at the time.

12:23.590 --> 12:26.320
I had no connections, so people 
turned me down all the time.

12:26.320 --> 12:29.350
My daily routine was to forcefully 
negotiate as much as I could.

12:29.350 --> 12:33.500
Yes, and that's why you 
have such a strong alibi.

12:33.500 --> 12:35.650
If you easily backed down in negotiations,

12:35.650 --> 12:39.270
you may have gotten time to 
go to the scene of the crime.

12:39.270 --> 12:41.780
You should always do your best at your job.

12:42.050 --> 12:44.320
Kaoruko-san had hurt her left leg,

12:44.320 --> 12:49.270
so she had canceled her plans for the day 
and was at Koya-san's condo by herself.

12:49.270 --> 12:53.540
Apparently, Kaoruko had taken quite a tumble 
in front of the condo that afternoon.

12:53.540 --> 12:57.330
She was resting in the room, but the 
swelling in her leg got worse that evening,

12:57.560 --> 13:00.100
so I took her to the hospital that night.

13:00.100 --> 13:02.860
We found out that her 
left tibia was fractured,

13:02.860 --> 13:04.550
and she was hospitalized that night.

13:04.550 --> 13:09.380
And because of her accident, 
Kaoruko-san was cleared of suspicion.

13:09.380 --> 13:14.500
There was no way she could attack 
Sumi-san and kill her with that leg.

13:14.500 --> 13:16.100
What good fortune for her.

13:16.410 --> 13:17.850
<b>Otonashi Family Inheritance 
Assignment Documents</b>

13:16.810 --> 13:17.850
Iwanaga-san.

13:17.850 --> 13:19.610
Just what are you trying to say?

13:20.590 --> 13:24.900
My grandfather was looking for the right 
moment when everyone else had an alibi,

13:24.900 --> 13:26.840
and killed my grandmother then?

13:26.840 --> 13:28.740
Isn't that a bit malicious to say?

13:28.740 --> 13:32.710
Everyone but Aunt Kaoruko knew about 
my grandfather's murder plot,

13:32.710 --> 13:35.860
and deliberately made sure they had 
an alibi at the time of the crime.

13:35.860 --> 13:37.370
That's what I'm hearing from you.

13:37.370 --> 13:40.630
Oh, I'd never do anything so distasteful.

13:40.890 --> 13:43.630
I did indeed propose an alliance,

13:43.630 --> 13:49.260
but despite your claims of selflessness, 
I never thought it'd be resolved so quickly.

13:49.260 --> 13:53.020
The inheritance is worth a large sum, 
and it also involves how the group is run.

13:53.020 --> 13:56.780
And Kaoruko-san and Ryoma-san, who are 
both part of this matter, are not present,

13:56.780 --> 13:58.560
so I thought you'd want to give it more time.

13:58.560 --> 14:01.810
It's as though you've 
settled this matter before

14:01.810 --> 14:04.440
any of your personal inconveniences came up.

14:04.830 --> 14:07.950
This alliance goes against 
President Otonashi's wishes,

14:07.950 --> 14:12.550
so if there were no apprehensions, 
I figured things would go earnestly.

14:13.090 --> 14:15.990
It could be you all had 
alibis coincidentally.

14:15.990 --> 14:17.370
But at the time of the incident,

14:17.620 --> 14:20.180
Ryoma-san, Susumu-san, Koya-san,

14:20.180 --> 14:22.580
and President Otonashi could 
have been conspiring together,

14:22.580 --> 14:25.130
so they made sure each alibi stuck.

14:25.420 --> 14:29.890
Kaoruko-san wasn't informed about any of 
this, so she almost didn't have an alibi.

14:30.210 --> 14:32.970
Wouldn't that interpretation 
be much more entertaining?

14:33.980 --> 14:36.310
I have no interest in the inheritance.

14:36.310 --> 14:37.390
My uncles have decided that

14:37.390 --> 14:41.100
my grandfather would not do anything 
irrational regarding the inheritance,

14:41.100 --> 14:43.410
and that it would be better for them

14:43.410 --> 14:46.000
to go along with your plan 
than to bicker amongst family.

14:46.000 --> 14:48.950
And yet, you have the nerve to mock 
this and call it entertaining?

14:49.320 --> 14:50.950
You truly lack any taste!

14:54.370 --> 14:57.880
If the four including my grandfather 
are indeed accomplices,

14:57.880 --> 15:00.330
there's no point to either this 
alliance or the assignment!

15:00.560 --> 15:04.070
Because my uncles would know that 
my grandfather is an accomplice.

15:04.070 --> 15:07.800
Correct. I do not believe that 
they are all accomplices.

15:08.100 --> 15:10.750
President Otonashi denies that, as well.

15:10.750 --> 15:12.510
But the president did say that

15:12.510 --> 15:15.220
the crime should get the proper punishment.

15:17.150 --> 15:20.130
Is Dad trying to get me to confess?

15:20.820 --> 15:23.010
Is that the purpose of this assignment?

15:23.500 --> 15:24.630
Uncle?

15:26.610 --> 15:27.430
Huh?

15:27.430 --> 15:28.360
I can't say.

15:28.610 --> 15:31.360
Even preparing for a murder 
would be considered a crime.

15:31.360 --> 15:33.530
Very well. I'll admit it.

15:33.530 --> 15:38.620
Twenty-three years ago, my brother and I 
came up with a plan to kill our mother.

15:39.610 --> 15:45.060
Mother was killed while we were still 
planning, so we never carried it out.

15:45.060 --> 15:49.930
With my dad? But you two haven't been 
on good terms for over thirty years!

15:49.930 --> 15:51.630
You were even arguing 
on the day of the murder!

15:51.630 --> 15:53.580
It's because they get along so terribly

15:53.580 --> 15:56.120
that no one would suspect 
they were accomplices.

15:56.120 --> 15:59.860
But their interests fundamentally aligned.

15:59.860 --> 16:02.640
So you've seen through everything, after all.

16:02.870 --> 16:03.880
On the day of the crime,

16:03.880 --> 16:07.840
you two were arguing 
so loudly that others noticed.

16:07.840 --> 16:10.030
That's why you had a solid alibi.

16:10.030 --> 16:13.910
But what if you were actually accomplices 
just <i>acting</i> like you were arguing?

16:14.180 --> 16:17.950
For example, if you two were alone 
arguing in a meeting room,

16:17.950 --> 16:20.910
perhaps everyone around you just 
heard voices and noises from outside.

16:21.260 --> 16:24.170
Or you could've played 
something recorded prior,

16:24.170 --> 16:26.050
<i>I don't want to do this.</i>

16:24.410 --> 16:26.040
and acted like you were fighting

16:26.040 --> 16:28.390
even though only one of you was in the room,

16:26.050 --> 16:27.920
<i>You don't understand anything, Nii-san!</i>

16:27.920 --> 16:29.650
<i>What do you mean by that?</i>

16:28.390 --> 16:30.670
making people think you were both there.

16:29.650 --> 16:30.670
<i>You've always been like this!</i>

16:31.130 --> 16:33.920
In the meantime, the other 
carries out the murder.

16:33.920 --> 16:36.940
Yes. That's how our alibis worked out.

16:38.220 --> 16:39.060
Nii-san.

16:39.410 --> 16:42.190
What do you want? Why'd you call me here?

16:42.840 --> 16:45.060
I figured you're the only 
one I could ask to do this.

16:45.350 --> 16:50.340
At this rate, our futures, as well 
as the group's, will be ruined.

16:51.050 --> 16:53.180
So we're going to kill Mom.

16:53.740 --> 16:56.740
All you need to do is help 
me come up with our alibis.

16:57.020 --> 16:58.830
I'll do all the dirty work.

16:59.710 --> 17:01.370
So you have a plan...

17:01.640 --> 17:04.210
Overall, the plan was as you described it.

17:04.600 --> 17:07.790
But we needed a few more tricks to 
make sure no one else suspected.

17:08.620 --> 17:10.790
Wait, are they fighting?

17:11.110 --> 17:14.420
I thought their relationship 
had gotten worse lately, but...

17:14.420 --> 17:16.760
Uh, someone should probably stop them.

17:16.990 --> 17:21.210
It wasn't unusual for my brother 
and me to fight at the office,

17:21.210 --> 17:24.810
so even if some people realized 
we were fighting in a room,

17:24.810 --> 17:26.520
it'd be better to stay out of it.

17:26.910 --> 17:29.770
That's the atmosphere we
were trying to create.

17:30.330 --> 17:32.530
Chief Otonashi, it's awful!

17:32.530 --> 17:33.630
The president...

17:34.180 --> 17:37.030
That was the day that 
our mother was murdered,

17:37.320 --> 17:42.230
and that was the fight that became our alibi 
twenty-three years ago on February 18th.

17:43.700 --> 17:47.250
Have you ever suspected that it was 
President Otonashi who committed the murder?

17:47.250 --> 17:50.640
Yes, but Dad had an alibi,

17:50.640 --> 17:53.230
and there were no signs that he hired 
anyone to carry out the killing.

17:53.230 --> 17:56.760
That's why our mother's death was just 
considered a burglary and murder.

17:57.030 --> 17:59.030
And now, this assignment.

17:59.030 --> 18:00.760
If our father isn't the murderer,

18:00.760 --> 18:02.380
I can't help but feel like 
he wanted us to confess

18:02.380 --> 18:04.390
that my brother and I plotted 
the murder in the past,

18:04.650 --> 18:07.890
and atone for our crime.

18:08.450 --> 18:10.520
Nii-san might've realized it, as well.

18:10.520 --> 18:15.110
Perhaps he sent Rion here 
to let her know of his crime

18:15.110 --> 18:17.780
and try to atone for it in some way.

18:18.780 --> 18:20.120
Wait, are you saying...

18:20.120 --> 18:23.660
that you and my father kept 
acting like you hated each other

18:23.660 --> 18:26.670
so no one would suspect that you 
were accomplices this whole time?

18:26.670 --> 18:30.380
Don't get the wrong idea. 
I do hate my brother.

18:30.670 --> 18:34.450
Nii-san threw aside the job I wanted 
and went off to do his own thing.

18:34.450 --> 18:37.840
Even though he was always 
better at this job than I was.

18:37.840 --> 18:41.010
I always felt inferior next to him...

18:42.070 --> 18:44.060
But I feel a bit better now.

18:44.290 --> 18:48.360
I'm grateful that I was given the 
opportunity to confess this.

18:48.730 --> 18:52.020
Now, how about Koya-san and Kaoruko-san?

18:52.310 --> 18:55.930
Did you also plot to 
murder Otonashi Sumi-san?

18:55.930 --> 18:59.150
The timing of Kaoruko-san's 
injury is far too convenient,

18:59.500 --> 19:02.660
so I tried to come up with this false alibi.

19:02.910 --> 19:04.910
The afternoon of the day of the murder,

19:04.910 --> 19:06.790
Kaoruko-san purposely 
fell in front of people,

19:07.200 --> 19:09.110
and acted like she'd hurt her leg.

19:09.110 --> 19:11.670
At that point, she hadn't really hurt 
herself, let alone broken anything.

19:11.970 --> 19:14.040
She then left the condo that evening,

19:14.310 --> 19:17.510
and murdered Sumi-san, 
making it look like a burglary.

19:17.510 --> 19:21.760
After that, she returned to the 
condo and fractured her leg herself.

19:22.760 --> 19:26.470
That's how she made it look like she had 
actually fractured her leg that afternoon,

19:26.470 --> 19:28.520
to make people believe she couldn't 
have committed the murder.

19:28.520 --> 19:30.090
That's quite the imagination.

19:30.090 --> 19:33.750
My leg hurt just hearing that.

19:33.750 --> 19:35.900
But even if she had hidden her face,

19:36.140 --> 19:39.110
there's no way she wouldn't 
recognize her own daughter.

19:39.110 --> 19:43.160
We know from Sumi-san's final 
screams that the suspect was a man.

19:43.160 --> 19:47.160
She said, "Someone catch 
that man in black!"

19:47.160 --> 19:51.160
But were those screams truly from Sumi-san?

19:51.440 --> 19:54.880
I don't think the residents in the area 
knew what Sumi-san sounded like.

19:54.880 --> 19:57.170
What if, in order to make people 
think the culprit was a man,

19:57.170 --> 19:59.450
Kaoruko-san acted like Sumi-san and

19:59.450 --> 20:03.050
screamed near her corpse 
to make sure people heard?

20:03.050 --> 20:05.860
That's far too risky a plot.

20:05.860 --> 20:08.550
If one of the residents had immediately 
come out after hearing the screams,

20:08.550 --> 20:10.610
Kaoruko would've been found.

20:10.610 --> 20:11.730
Indeed.

20:12.010 --> 20:15.220
I mean, if you plotted a 
murder in a residential area,

20:15.220 --> 20:18.400
you'd have to make sure the victim 
couldn't speak when the murder happened,

20:18.400 --> 20:21.290
and the murderer would probably make sure

20:21.290 --> 20:24.030
there was no evidence left 
before leaving the scene.

20:25.020 --> 20:25.780
But...

20:25.780 --> 20:27.500
This is your golden opportunity.

20:27.500 --> 20:31.190
According to Susumu-san, this might 
be your chance to feel a bit better.

20:32.140 --> 20:35.420
Very well, I'll come 
clean. It's the opposite.

20:35.640 --> 20:39.250
It's not that Kaoruko broke her leg, 
and then the murder was committed.

20:39.250 --> 20:42.800
She broke her leg, and it 
messed up our murder plot.

20:44.130 --> 20:47.890
Kaoruko and I were indeed 
plotting her mother's murder.

20:48.520 --> 20:50.720
We even plotted to murder her on 
her way home from her massage,

20:50.720 --> 20:52.270
just like Susumu-san and Ryoma-san.

20:52.270 --> 20:56.120
That was the only time she was ever alone.

20:56.120 --> 20:59.020
And on that day, we were 
going to carry out our plot.

20:59.360 --> 21:03.110
We did indeed plan to mislead the 
time she broke her leg, as you said.

21:03.110 --> 21:07.130
On the day of the incident, 
in order to fabricate my alibi,

21:07.130 --> 21:09.080
I had been running around, 
negotiating all day,

21:09.080 --> 21:11.330
and returned to the condo that night.

21:11.330 --> 21:14.710
Kaoruko should've already carried 
out the murder at that point.

21:17.800 --> 21:18.840
Kaoruko?

21:21.290 --> 21:23.290
Koya-san, I'm sorry.

21:24.140 --> 21:25.930
I messed up...

21:25.930 --> 21:27.010
Kaoruko!

21:27.400 --> 21:31.890
When I made it look like I fell this 
afternoon, I apparently really broke my leg.

21:32.600 --> 21:34.180
I'm such a fool!

21:34.180 --> 21:37.860
Even if I can still ambush her, 
I can't run after her like this!

21:37.860 --> 21:40.620
There was no way I could kill her and run.

21:41.410 --> 21:45.360
We found out about her mother's death 
at the hospital I took Kaoruko to.

21:45.360 --> 21:48.240
Someone had killed her.

21:48.240 --> 21:52.260
If this was providence from the 
heavens, it definitely felt eerie.

21:52.590 --> 21:55.630
I thought that maybe President 
Otonashi had figured out our plot

21:55.630 --> 21:59.960
and decided to carry it out earlier, 
but we just went on living our lives,

21:59.960 --> 22:01.750
knowing we had been spared.

22:01.970 --> 22:04.070
And then this assignment happened.

22:04.070 --> 22:08.380
We wondered if he was trying to get 
us to confess our past sins, as well.

22:08.720 --> 22:12.990
Kaoruko has been scared ever since, 
so I had to be the one to show up.

22:12.990 --> 22:19.150
But I never dreamed that Ryoma-san and 
Susumu-san had also planned to murder her.

22:19.150 --> 22:21.980
Perhaps the president also felt as 
though he didn't have much time left

22:21.980 --> 22:24.780
and wanted to square away his past.

22:25.030 --> 22:29.280
Maybe he wanted us to confess our sins 
to lighten the burden on our backs.

22:31.020 --> 22:32.530
Well, Miss Iwanaga?

22:32.850 --> 22:35.370
The sins of the successors have come to light.

22:35.370 --> 22:37.450
We can end this farce now, can't we?

22:38.040 --> 22:39.710
But it's not over.

22:40.810 --> 22:46.590
I have no interest in what you all were 
doing at the time, or hearing you repent.

22:46.940 --> 22:50.590
It's already past the statute of limitations, 
and it's not fundamentally the issue at hand.

22:50.820 --> 22:54.220
How did President Otonashi kill 
Otonashi Sumi-san at the time?

22:54.220 --> 22:57.020
That's the answer he would like to hear.

22:57.240 --> 22:59.770
All of your sins are trivial.

23:00.180 --> 23:01.300
Then why in the world

23:01.300 --> 23:04.570
did you have us all admit that we 
plotted to murder our mother?

23:04.570 --> 23:08.610
You were all so concerned with how you 
were going to conceal your crimes,

23:08.610 --> 23:11.360
you didn't prepare for the 
actual answer, did you?

23:11.600 --> 23:14.520
I'm certain that Rion-san 
couldn't concentrate with all

23:14.520 --> 23:16.330
the secrets that were in the air.

23:16.600 --> 23:20.000
That's why I figured, if that wasn't taken 
care of first, we couldn't get started.

23:20.000 --> 23:24.670
I was chosen to judge this, so I must make 
sure this task is carried out properly.

23:24.670 --> 23:28.160
President Otonashi wants 
his past success that

23:28.160 --> 23:30.630
stemmed from someone else's 
death to be corrected.

23:30.630 --> 23:34.910
Success sometimes harms people and 
leads them to their own destruction.

23:34.910 --> 23:37.750
That's why it was necessary 
to correct the past.

23:38.570 --> 23:39.540
Now, then...

23:39.540 --> 23:44.690
There is an answer as to how 
President Otonashi killed Sumi-san.

23:44.690 --> 23:46.180
Please think carefully.

23:47.020 --> 23:50.050
To be continued
